nt\'s range is wide, but betting out of position ("donk betting") with only middle pair creates a risk of being raised or called by a better hand (like an Ace).\n\nReason: Acting first on the flop with a marginal hand like middle pair, the best strategy is usually to Check. This keeps the pot small (pot control) and allows you to induce bluffs or see a cheaper showdown. If you bet, you likely only get called by hands that beat you (like an Ace) and fold out hands that you are beating. Checking preserves your chip stack while maintaining the opportunity to call a reasonable bet or see a free Turn card.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
